abstract:
  File format identification is generally accepted as a key digital
  preservation activity as it enables preservation practitioners to
  understand, manage, and mitigate format-related risks and challenges.
  This foundational workshop will explore the concepts and practical
  approaches to file format identification. The workshop assumes no
  prior knowledge or experience of file format identification, and aims
  to cater to different learning styles with a selection of interactive
  activities.
